---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Vivero Mar Azul — Sustainable Nursery at Mar Azul Costa Rica | Coyol Real Estate">
  <article class="blog-post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <p class="category">Sustainability</p>
      <h1>Vivero Mar Azul</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">De la semilla a tu hogar — where restaurant waste becomes living soil</p>
      <time datetime="2026-08-07">August 7, 2026</time>
    </header>

    <figure class="hero-image">
      <img src="/images/mar-azul/vivero/hero.jpg" alt="Vivero Mar Azul nursery" />
      <figcaption>Vivero Mar Azul — growing native plants in living soil</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p class="lead">In the hills behind Nosara, something remarkable is happening. The vegetable scraps from last night's dinner at La Luna, the organic waste from Coyol's kitchen, the coffee grounds from Esh bakery — all of it is being transformed into something extraordinary. At Vivero Mar Azul, waste becomes life.</p>

      <p>The nursery, nestled within the Mar Azul development, operates on a simple but powerful principle: every plant is grown from seed, nurtured in living soil made from organic compost collected from the Meraki restaurant group. No synthetic fertilizers. No imported growing media. Just patience, microorganisms, and a closed-loop system that turns one business's waste into another's foundation.</p>

      <blockquote>
        "Plantas sanas. Suelo vivo. Hogares más verdes."<br>
        <span style="font-style: normal;">Healthy plants. Living soil. Greener homes.</span>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>The Process</h2>
      
      <p>It begins in the kitchens. Every day, organic residues — vegetable trimmings, fruit peels, eggshells — are collected from La Luna and Coyol. From Esh bakery, the coffee grounds. What was once waste becomes raw material.</p>

      <p>Back at the nursery, these materials are combined with microorganisms we cultivate in-house in 200-liter drums. The process is anaerobic, slow, and deliberate — developed over years of experimentation in the hills of Guanacaste. No shortcuts. No synthetic accelerants.</p>

      <p>The result is a living compost, rich with beneficial bacteria and fungi. When we sow seeds into this tierra viva, they emerge stronger — nutrient-dense plants that thrive without chemical fertilizers.</p>

      <figure class="inline-image">
        <img src="/images/mar-azul/vivero/greenhouse.jpg" alt="Greenhouse at Vivero Mar Azul" />
        <figcaption>The greenhouse at Vivero Mar Azul, where seedlings grow in living soil</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="stats-block">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="number">🌱</span>
          <span class="label">Desde la Semilla — Every plant grown from seed</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="number">♻️</span>
          <span class="label">Tierra Viva — Living soil from restaurant compost</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="number">🏡</span>
          <span class="label">Nuevos Hogares — Native plants for Mar Azul homes</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Native, Sustainable, Local</h2>
      
      <p>The nursery focuses on native Guanacaste species — plants that have evolved over millennia to thrive in this climate. They need little irrigation once established. They support local pollinators. They belong here.</p>

      <p>For the residents of Mar Azul, this means gardens that arrive already adapted to their new home. Plants that know this soil, this rainfall pattern, this dry season. Gardens that connect the dinner table to the earth and back again.</p>

      <h2>A Circular Economy</h2>
      
      <p>What makes this project significant isn't just the plants — it's the philosophy. In a region where development often means extraction, Vivero Mar Azul demonstrates another way. Waste becomes resource. Restaurants feed nurseries. Nurseries feed homes. Homes, eventually, might feed restaurants again.</p>

      <p>It's a small loop, but a complete one. And in that completion, there's something worth paying attention to.</p>

      <p style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: #666; margin-top: 3rem;">
        Cuidamos la tierra · Apoyamos a nuestra comunidad · Transformamos residuos en vida
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="post-footer">
      <div class="tags">
        <span>Tags:</span>
        <a href="/blog/tag/sustainability">Sustainability</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/mar-azul">Mar Azul</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/nosara">Nosara</a>
        <a href="/blog/tag/gardening">Gardening</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-post {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .post-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .category {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #3D4F3D;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .post-header h1 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #666;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  time {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #999;
  }

  .hero-image {
    margin: 0 -2rem 3rem;
  }

  .hero-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .hero-image figcaption,
  .inline-image figcaption {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #666;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .post-content {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #333;
  }

  .post-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .post-content h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 3rem 0 1.5rem;
    color: #1a1a1a;
  }

  blockquote {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #3D4F3D;
    border-left: 3px solid #3D4F3D;
    padding: 1rem 0 1rem 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .inline-image {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .inline-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .stats-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 2rem;
    background: #f9f9f7;
    border: 1px solid #e8e6e3;
  }

  .stat {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .stat .number {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .stat .label {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #666;
  }

  .post-footer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #e8e6e3;
  }

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .tags span {
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }

  .tags a {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #3D4F3D;
    background: #f0f0f0;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .tags a:hover {
    background: #3D4F3D;
    color: white;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .post-header h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .hero-image {
      margin: 0 -1rem 2rem;
    }

    .stats-block {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
